The spoken audio is generated locally from the German quest text with
Chatterbox Multilingual (Resemble AI), whose code and model weights are both
released under the MIT License. That is why it was chosen: the audio it
produces can be redistributed with this addon.

The German quest text is Blizzard Entertainment's, read from the World of
Warcraft Game Data API under the project's own credentials. No third-party
content dump is used anywhere in this project.

The narrator voice is cloned from a recording by Thorsten Müller, from the
Thorsten-Voice German neutral corpus (OpenSLR 95, https://www.openslr.org/95/),
a corpus he released so that others could build German speech with it. OpenSLR
states CC0; Zenodo's metadata for the same corpus says CC BY 4.0, so it is
attributed here either way.

Other reference recordings are not part of this repository. Each voice records
where its reference came from; see voices/README.md for what may and may not be
used.

